  keep  thinking we need to remember you know  this is very much in the civilian  consumer space it's affecting real  people  and they're in in their ordinary lives  now the safest way to bank is from home  at lloyd's bank there's so much you can  do to manage your money online  from viewing statements to managing  direct debits to paying bills  you can speak to a mortgage advisor by  video or over the phone  and even pay in checks using our app if  you do need to visit most branches are  open 9 30 till 2 monday to friday  please wear a face covering and observe  social distancing to protect yourself  and our colleagues  lloyd's bank by your side terms and  conditions apply  on the 19th of december 2017 the uk  and the us accused north korea of  unleashing the wannacry attack  a year later the u.s justice department  charged a north korean man with alleged  involvement  in a series of cyber attacks including  wannacry  and also the hack against sony pictures  that we covered in episode three  pyongyang has strongly denied the  allegations  i asked marcus hutchins how stopping a  suspected north korean cyber attack had  changed his life  so i'd always been fairly anonymous i  didn't  really publish my real name or identity  because i like to just have  a pseudonym so  about a day after wannacry the media  actually found out who i was and  published my real name and my location  in the paper  so i kind of went from uh like my online  name was known but  my real identity was very unknown and i  went in a day from  being this kind of unknown name to my  my face and my my name and my location  is plastered all over the news across  the world  and how was that uh it was it was not  fun  yeah and were you uh were you living  with your parents at the time  yeah i was so what do they make did they  know that you were this kind of  tech tech genius i wouldn't say genius  but they  they knew i was into tech and they knew  i kind of worked in uh  in security they didn't know a 